======================================================================================================
Route slugs were already English and German route names are already handled (existing redirects in astro.config.mjs, e.g. /berufe -> /english-for-work); nothing renamed.
Fragment ids translated (hash links, ids and the tab alias in skills.astro; old #hoeren/#lesen/#schreiben/#sprechen still work): /skills#hoeren -> #listening, #sprechen -> #speaking (+ #reading, #writing),
  #niveau-x -> #level-x, #gruppe-<id> -> #group-<id>, #bestenliste -> #leaderboard (games; API path /api/*/bestenliste untouched), #offiziell -> #official. 20 files; no page moved, so no redirects needed.
VERIFICATION: pnpm build ok (1700 pages), pnpm check:base ok. (The existing `pnpm check:links` reports 2 links from /english/ to /espanol/ and /francais/ as "outside /english": pre-existing, they are the course cross-links.)
LEFTOVERS: German fragment/data ids remain (#grammatik-start, #grammatik-a1, #wortschatz-b1 download ids, #klassensatz, #pk-parlamente, #l5/#schreiben/#h1 exam task ids, #labyrinth on /intonation);
  data links to /politik, /steueroasen and /merch (the first two have redirects in astro.config.mjs, /merch has no page); src/oldux/* still holds old German tab ids.
  Other lanes' uncommitted changes in apps/english were left in place.

OVERALL NOTES
- Nothing committed; renames are staged by `git mv` only. Scratch tooling (map files, generator for legacy-redirects.json) lives in the session scratchpad, not in the repo; the JSON files are the result.
- Do not run two builds of one app at the same time (shared dist/.prerender): it corrupts both.
- To keep Spanish/French parallel: Spanish section names mirror the French ones in meaning (competences=habilidades, ecoute=comprension-auditiva, ...), fragments follow the same scheme, redirects use the same JSON + _redirects mechanism as lane B.
